  "caption": "Quinn read the scan report at midnight, saw the word \"slipped\" and imagined a spine sliding away. Real life: a bit of ache with long standing that eases with sitting.\n\nLow-grade slips are often stable, many people with one have no pain, and most don't progress in adulthood. Symptoms tend to guide the plan more than the grade.\n\nWhat often helps: regular walking, building trunk, hip and glute strength, easing off big back-bends during flare-ups rather than stopping everything, and gradually returning to what you enjoy.\n\nProgressive leg weakness or numbness, or leg pain on walks that eases with sitting, are worth getting checked. Bladder or bowel changes need urgent medical review.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
